  PregFaq(
    id: 'PREG-EMOTION-014',
    number: 280,
    month: 7,
    question: 'How can I manage anxiety about labour and the road ahead?',
    category: 'Mental & Emotional Wellbeing',
    applicability: 'Month 7 onward (third trimester)',
    canI: 'Not applicable',
    sensitivity: 'Yes (light)',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Feeling anxious about labour as the third trimester begins is extremely common; this is genuinely different from earlier pregnancy anxiety, which often centred on miscarriage or screening results. Talking openly about specific fears, staying informed through antenatal classes, and leaning on your support system all help.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.why, '', [
        'As your due date starts to feel real rather than distant, it\'s natural for your mind to turn toward the unknowns ahead, labour itself, whether you\'ll cope, whether your baby will be okay. Naming a specific fear out loud is often far more manageable than a vague, general sense of dread, which tends to feel bigger the longer it stays unspoken.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Antenatal classes genuinely help here, turning abstract fears into concrete, familiar information. Talking to your partner, a friend who\'s given birth, or a doctor about your specific worries, rather than carrying them alone, tends to help most. Mindfulness or simple guided relaxation can also ease the emotional weight day to day.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'If anxiety feels overwhelming or is affecting your sleep, appetite, or daily functioning, mention this to your doctor; support beyond simply pushing through is available.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'Feeling nervous about something this significant isn\'t a sign you\'re unprepared; it\'s simply a natural response to something genuinely big, and it doesn\'t mean you won\'t handle it well.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'Labour-related anxiety is common and different from earlier pregnancy worries.',
        'Naming a specific fear helps more than sitting with vague dread.',
