    month: 7,
    question: 'When should I actually start my maternity leave?',
    category: 'Work & Travel',
    applicability: 'Month 7 onward',
    canI: 'Do',
    sensitivity: 'No',
    parts: [
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.direct, '', [
        'Under India\'s Maternity Benefit Act, you can take up to 8 weeks of your leave before your due date, but you\'re not required to start that early; some women prefer to work closer to their due date, others prefer more time to rest beforehand. This is a personal decision based on your job\'s physical demands and how you\'re feeling.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.whyMatters, '', [
        'If your work is physically demanding, stressful, or involves long hours, standing, or travel, starting leave a week or two before your due date can genuinely help ensure a calmer final stretch. If your role allows work-from-home or is less physically taxing, working closer to your due date, and saving more leave for after delivery, is equally reasonable.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.forYou, '', [
        'Give your employer written notice stating your expected delivery date and when you plan to start your leave, ideally with enough lead time for a smooth handover. There\'s no single right answer here; weigh your specific job demands, how your pregnancy is going, and how much time you\'d rather have with your baby afterward.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.doctor, '', [
        'Ask your doctor if your specific pregnancy or job situation suggests starting leave earlier than you\'d otherwise planned.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.perspective, '', [
        'This decision is entirely yours to make; there\'s no more "correct" way to split your leave than there is a single right way to experience these final weeks.',
      ], []),
      PregFaqPart(PregFaqSection.takeaways, '', [], [
        'You can take up to 8 weeks of leave before your due date, but aren\'t required to.',
        'Physically demanding or stressful jobs may benefit from starting earlier.',
        'Work-from-home or less demanding roles allow more flexibility to work later.',
        'Give your employer written notice with your expected delivery date.',
        'This is a personal decision based on your job and how you\'re feeling.',
      ]),
    ],
